;; (this rung's own scoped decode proves it: ForwardProp completes across
;; the whole function with zero remaining type-prop errors), but the
;; later types2 pass still throws "TP_Type::get_slot failed: 128"
;; building the final expression tree from the spilled value. This is
;; the same decompiler-internal spill-tracking wall already documented on
;; (method 10 minimap) and (method 11 minimap) in hacks.jsonc (hand-
;; casting every reload clears the reported errors but leaves types2
;; unable to finish); a stack_structures.jsonc declaration for the spill
;; offset was not attempted here since minimap's own attempt at the
;; analogous fix aborted outright with a different crash, and disabling
;; type analysis for the whole method (hacks.jsonc's
;; no_type_analysis_functions_by_name) was tried and rejected: it trades
;; this failure for an earlier one ("didn't know its type"), producing no
;; usable body at all rather than a degraded one. Retirement condition:
;; a decompiler fix for cross-branch stack-spill type tracking, or a
;; verified-safe hand transcription of the raw MIPS body (not attempted
;; this rung given its size, dozens of branches over roughly 700 atomic
;; ops). Until then hud-results falls back to hud-item-group's own
;; generic method 19; the retail per-message-id text/texture updates this
;; override drives do not fire.

